#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run a managed workflow, check its status, result, and logs, find the cause "
"of an error, and cancel a job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run a managed workflow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/run-managed-workflow.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore maxwait squeue scancel */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A managed workflow job works like a batch job that you submit to an HPC scheduler. `run()` submits the job and returns a `Job` object immediately. Use the `Job` object for the tasks that `squeue`, the job's output file, and `scancel` cover on a cluster. The job keeps running after you close your notebook.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The examples on this page use a small workflow that reads one angle, "
"`theta`, and fails if the angle is out of range. Upload it as described in "
"[Deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-"
"workflow).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Start a job {#start-a-job}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Get the workflow by its title, and call `run()` with the arguments that the "
"workflow reads:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`run()` returns after the workflow queues the job. Save the job ID so that "
"you can [find the job from a new session](#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To choose which arguments a workflow accepts and check them before the job "
"starts, see [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-"
"outputs).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To run the job on a different compute size, pass `function_size`. See "
"[Choose a size for each run](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-"
"profiles#choose-a-size-for-each-run).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Follow a job {#follow-a-job}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` "
"returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as"
" `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the "
"final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you "
"set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` "
"when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 "
"seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within"
" seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval"
" instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes "
"to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, "
"before it has a result:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time"
" when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, "
"`job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at"
" the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-"
"workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a "
"regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, "
"pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with"
" no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, "
"`job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without "
"waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job "
"ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and "
"`SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of"
" a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-"
"run).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-"
"workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read "
"them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with "
"`job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, "
"`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and "
"`job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not "
"recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside "
"gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the "
"entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether "
"custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should "
"return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU "
"jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), "
"which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends "
"`SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a "
"job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-"
"job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job "
"already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went "
"to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint "
"finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes "
"during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it "
"with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or "
"`created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` "
"and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call "
"`client.list()`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM "
"Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, "
"and run times.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the "
"job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to "
"file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-"
"checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from "
"its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py "
"stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create "
"events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This "
"looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) to set up the logs and errors that a job reports.\n"
"- [Run a parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) to run the workflow one time for each set of inputs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
